  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing access of refugees to labour mobility pathways through skills development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to equip refugees in Malaysia with the skills and certifications needed to access regular labour migration pathways beyond Malaysia. By mapping labour migration opportunities from Malaysia to target destination countries, the project generates evidence to inform policies and programmes on regular migration pathways. In partnership with local training institutions, it will deliver demand-driven skills training aligned with labour market needs in key industrial sectors abroad. Expected outcomes include enhanced refugee employability and improved access to labour migration opportunities in destination countries, as well as strengthened institutional capacity in Malaysia to provide market-responsive skills development. The project contributes to SDGs 8, 9, 10, and 17 by promoting decent work, reducing inequalities, and fostering cross-sector partnerships to advance refugee inclusion.</narrative>
  </description>
